==English==
{{was wotd|2015|October|27}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|miscellanées}}, from {{der|en|la|miscellanea}}, from {{m|la|miscellus||mixed}}, from {{m|la|misceō||to mix}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/mɪˈsɛləni/|/ˈmɪsələni/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-miscellany.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪsəleɪni/|/mɪˈsɛləni/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-miscellany.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[assortment]] of [[miscellaneous]] items.
#: {{syn|en|miscellanea|smorgasbord|Thesaurus:hodgepodge}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A collection of writings on various [[subject]]s or [[topic]]s; an [[anthology]].
#: {{syn|en|reader}}
#: ''a monthly '''miscellany''' of literature''
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The condition of being miscellaneous, of being a [[hodgepodge]].
#: {{syn|en|miscellaneousness}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1896|month=March|author=w:Louis H. Sullivan|title=The Tall Office Building Artistically Considered|journal={{w|Lippincott's Monthly Magazine|Lippincott’s Monthly Magazine}}|volume=57|page=407|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=RAhqP9B8h0wC&pg=PA407|text=All of these critics and theorists agree, however, positively, unequivocally, in this, {{...}} that '''miscellany''' is abhorrent to their sense; that the sixteen-story building must not consist of sixteen separate, distinct, and unrelated buildings piled one upon the other until the top of the pile is reached.}}

